{{Passive skill box|Immortal Ambition}}
'''Immortal Ambition''' is a [[keystone passive skill]] which allows [[life]] [[leech]] to recover [[energy shield]] while on [[full life]], while disabling energy shield [[recharge]] and energy shield [[regeneration]], and causing 5% energy shield [[loss]] per second. 

This keystone is only accessible through certain unique items.

==Mechanics==
{{c|mod|Life Leech effects Recover Energy Shield instead while on Full Life}}:
* This does not create energy shield leech instances (unlike {{psl|Ghost Reaver}}); life leech effects remain life leech, and accordingly, are still based on maximum life, and modified by life leech modifiers.<ref name=Mark>{{cite web|url=https://www.reddit.com/r/pathofexile/comments/axcd00/how_do_you_calculate_the_cap_for_es_leech_with/|title=Re: How do you calculate the cap for ES leech? (with Ghost Reaver, Vaal Pact and Vixen's entrapment interactions)|author=Mark_GGG|publisher=Official Path of Exile subreddit|date=March 5, 2019|accessdate=March 21, 2021}}</ref>
* Energy shield recovery per second from life leech ''is'' limited by {{c|mod|Maximum total Energy Shield Recovery per second from Leech}} however, sharing this cap with regular energy shield leech. (By default 10% of maximum ES per second.) 
* Effects that cause life leech to recover life instantly (e.g. {{psl|Vaal Pact}}) will also cause ES to be recovered instantly. Instant recovery is not limited by the per-second recovery cap on ES, only by the per-instance cap of life leech (normally 10% of maximum life). When a hit's instant leech fills life, the remaining recovery will recover ES. 
* Life leech stops recovering life as soon as the player counts as on full life, including with modifiers like the {{c|mod|You count as on Full Life while at 90% of maximum Life or above}} [[Life Mastery]]. 
* Life [[reservation]] will normally prevent ES recovery, as the player will be unable to reach full life. 
* Life leech instances are not removed when energy shield is filled. 

==Location==
This keystone will conquer (i.e. convert) any existing keystones on the skill tree, that within the jewel radius of a {{il|Glorious Vanity}}. The jewel needs to have the modifier {{c|mod|Bathed in the blood of (100–8000) sacrificed in the name of '''Ahuana'''}}.

==Related unique items==
These [[unique item]]s (other than {{il|Glorious Vanity}}) have the {{c|mod|Immortal Ambition}} modifier, which provides the same effect as this keystone. Taking the keystone in addition to equipping one of these items will impart no additional benefit.
